848:After I injured myself during Taekwondo practice, Miss Chiori and I went to a pharmacy to get bandages.
849:Ah, I can't believe I didn't keep the receipt this time. How strange... It's obviously a precious memory with Miss Chiori, so how could I have lost it?!
850:As for the mask that made you suspect us...
851:Forget it! You're such a dumb detective! I don't even feel like telling you!
852:Not even now?!
853:Chiori Mikami gives Riu Kujou a nod, and the latter pulls open the cabinet to reveal a pile of vermillion bird masks...
854:!!!
855:The *inaudible* theater near the auction house hands out these masks to the audience. Everyone who's been there can have one...
856:Chiori Mikami whispers its name so softly I fail to hear it.
857:Which theater?
858:Its name isn't important. All you need to know is that the theater hands out these masks!
859:They hand out these ugly masks for every show! And my mother just happens to be really fond of going there every vacation...
860:I still need to know which theater it is. Please tell me, it's very important for my investigation!
861:Chiori Mikami gazes at me, purses her lips, then turns around and shouts at the top of her lungs.
862:You're so annoying! It's the children's theater! You just had to make me say it! I hate you, {var:player_nickname}! You are the worst! THE WORST!
863:Sorry...
864:It turns out it was all just a big misunderstanding.
865:Damn {var:player_nickname}! How could you suspect that I would wear this... this... this thing... and commit a robbery?!
866:I now know it wasn't you.
867:That isn't the issue! It's this ugly mask! I even suggested last year they change it to a bear! Why didn't they go with my idea?!
868:I now realize I wasn't the cause of Chiori Mikami's anger, it was mainly the mask... Now that I'm taking a closer look, it does look rather ugly.
869:It's almost nighttime by the time I finally manage to calm them down and leave Chiori Mikami's place.
870:Since so many people could have these masks, their value as evidence is rather limited. I take a look at the time and decide it would be wise to just continue my investigation tomorrow.
872:Bamboo Inn - Second Floor
876:Champion Auction House
877:The second floor is where the items up for auction are exhibited. Once we ascend the spiral staircase in the lobby, we notice that most of the display cabinets are intact, and only one by the window is open.
878:Champion Auction House - Second Floor
879:He was wearing a mask. I-I couldn't see his face... And his voice was really strange. It sounded like he was using a voice changer. His voice sounded kind of... kind of like a girl...
880:Ume frowns upon hearing this and quickly walks to the display cabinet. I follow suit, and notice a shallow, heart-shaped groove on the red silk in the cabinet.
881:Fine, I'll give it a try! I may not be a professional, but who knows? Maybe the criminal is even less professional.
882:Investigate the Auction House's front yard
889:That's all the strange things in this place. Well... Why is there soil here?
890:Beryl Blue
891:Fuuka Minami & Qing Luan
892:Um... Ahem, I'm here to ask about your visit to Champion Auction House yesterday...
893:I explain the whole situation to Qing Luan...
894:Ask Qing Luan
895:Which hint might be related to Qing Luan?
898:Qing Luan has nothing to do with this.
899:Qing Luan has something to do with this.
900:Chiori Mikami's House
901:(whisper) How long do you think Chiori will stay mad at me?
902:Riu Kujou sneaks a glance at Chiori Mikami, and then she confidently raises five fingers at me.
903:(whisper) Ten minutes?
904:(whisper) Ten... hours?
905:TEN DAYS?!
906:Maybe I can just whisper my questions and show the clues to Riu Kujou, and she can nod and shake her head to answer with a "yes" or "no," right?
907:Ask Riu Kujou
908:Which hint might be related to Chiori Mikami and Riu Kujou?
909:Did you attend yesterday's exhibition?
910:It isn't Riu, what about Chiori...
911:So where did you get that mask?
912:In that case...
913:Was it you?
914:Was it someone other than the two of you?
915:Hint [Receipt (Bandage)] has been resolved
920:You found some crumpled paper. It is a shopping receipt for bandages from a pharmacy, dated two days ago.
922:You found some crumpled paper. It is a shopping receipt for plaster from a hardware store, dated two days ago.
924:There appear to be some messy footprints on the wet mud in front of the entrance. Make an impression for further investigations.
925:I think that if you're here to convict me of a crime I did not commit, then this discussion is over.
926:I'm happy to make the introductions if you need a doctor, Ms. Minami.

930:Anyway, Riu, you believe me, right? I'm just an ordinary eyewitness turned detective, running around doing errands...
939:Ugh! Oww! I can't breathe!{var:ShakeScene}
940:This visit was literally a near-death experience, and it all began just ten minutes ago...
941:I'm so taken aback that I forget to keep my voice down, but Riu Kujou still... shakes her head.
